```java
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;

public class Hits {
    private final AtomicInteger hits = new AtomicInteger(); // many writers -> atomic
    private volatile boolean enabled = true;                // single-writer flag -> volatile

    public void record() { if (enabled) hits.incrementAndGet(); }
    public int total()   { return hits.get(); }
    public void disable(){ enabled = false; }
}
```

Rule of thumb: read-only flag -> volatile; shared counter -> AtomicInteger; multi-field invariant -> a lock.

